      "problem": "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n\nI. ${Q}^{-}$ (the set of negative rationals)\n\nII. ${Z}^{+}$ (the set of positive integers)\n\nIII. $N$",
      "worked_solution": "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{-}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every negative rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{+}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every positive integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III\".",
